# A capacitor and an inductor trading energy back and forth.
#
# The battery charges the capacitor through S1. Open S1 and close S2: the capacitor drives current
# through the inductor, which keeps it flowing after the capacitor is empty and charges it the other
# way round, again and again, at 1 / (2π √(LC)), about 5 kHz. The resistor in series loses a little
# energy each swing, so the ringing dies away.

speed 2m

battery   B1  0 0  0 6  5V
switch    S1  0 0  4 0  closed
capacitor C1  4 0  4 6  1u
switch    S2  4 0  8 0
resistor  R1  8 0  8 3  2
inductor  L1  8 3  8 6  1m
wire          8 6  0 6
ground        0 6
meter     V   4 0  4 6
